<section class="tk-home-editorial" id="tk-atelier-editorial" aria-labelledby="tk-home-editorial-title">
  <div class="tk-home-editorial__container">
    
    <!-- HEADER & DIRECT ANSWER (AEO / GEO CORE ENTITY DEFINITION) -->
    <header class="tk-home-editorial__header">
      <div class="tk-home-editorial__eyebrow">
        <span>✦ Timberkala Atelier · Handcrafted Indian Heritage ✦</span>
      </div>
      <h2 id="tk-home-editorial-title" class="tk-home-editorial__title">
        Handcrafted Wooden Home Decor Items &amp; Artisanal Living Room Artefacts
      </h2>
      
      <!-- AEO & GEO DIRECT ANSWER BOX -->
      <div class="tk-home-editorial__direct-answer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/AboutPage">
        <div class="tk-home-editorial__badge">✦ What is Timberkala? · Brand Entity Definition</div>
        <p class="tk-home-editorial__direct-answer-text" itemprop="description">
          <strong>Timberkala</strong> is an Indian artisanal luxury home decor atelier specializing in handcrafted wooden artefacts, molten glass on reclaimed teak roots, and sacred Vastu-compliant sculptures. Carved from 100% salvaged timber and seasoned hardwoods, Timberkala fuses centuries-old Indian woodcraft with contemporary wabi-sabi aesthetics, delivering organic warmth, biophilic grounding, and acoustic calm to modern urban homes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- 4 CRAFTSMANSHIP PILLARS -->
    <div class="tk-home-pillars">
      <div class="tk-home-pillar">
        <div class="tk-home-pillar__icon" aria-hidden="true">🌱</div>
        <div class="tk-home-pillar__content">
          <h3 class="tk-home-pillar__title">100% Salvaged Reclaimed Hardwood</h3>
          <p class="tk-home-pillar__desc">
            Sourced exclusively from decades-old teak roots, fallen timber, and dismantled structures. Zero live trees felled; 100% carbon-conscious sustainable luxury.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tk-home-pillar">
        <div class="tk-home-pillar__icon" aria-hidden="true">🔥</div>
        <div class="tk-home-pillar__content">
          <h3 class="tk-home-pillar__title">Molten Glass on Teak Root Art</h3>
          <p class="tk-home-pillar__desc">
            Hand-blown recycled glass slumped at 1,000°C directly onto live teak roots, capturing every crevice and fissure in an unrepeatable fusion of fire and earth.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tk-home-pillar">
        <div class="tk-home-pillar__icon" aria-hidden="true">🛡️</div>
        <div class="tk-home-pillar__content">
          <h3 class="tk-home-pillar__title">Natural Termite &amp; Borer Immunity</h3>
          <p class="tk-home-pillar__desc">
            Aged heartwood naturally saturated with Tectoquine preservative oils, providing permanent termite defense and hand-buffed with non-toxic organic beeswax.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="tk-home-pillar">
        <div class="tk-home-pillar__icon" aria-hidden="true">🧭</div>
        <div class="tk-home-pillar__content">
          <h3 class="tk-home-pillar__title">Vastu Shastra &amp; Biophilic Balance</h3>
          <p class="tk-home-pillar__desc">
            Tactile hardwood grains engineered to soften acoustic glare in glass-and-concrete flats while aligning positive cosmic prana in North and East domestic quadrants.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- EDITORIAL DEEP DIVE WITH ACCESSIBLE EXPANDER -->
    <div class="tk-home-editorial__narrative">
      <p class="tk-home-editorial__lead">
        In an era of mass-manufactured MDF furniture and cold synthetic composites, Timberkala restores soulful authenticity to Indian interiors. Every piece in our collection is sculpted by hereditary master woodcrafters, celebrating natural live edges, annular tree growth rings, and the timeless philosophy of <em>Wabi-Sabi</em>—finding sublime elegance in organic natural imperfections.
      </p>

      <div class="tk-home-editorial__expandable" id="tk-home-expandable-content">
        <div class="tk-home-editorial__section">
          <h3 class="tk-home-editorial__subtitle">Reviving Indian Heritage Woodturning for Contemporary Urban Living</h3>
          <p>
            Modern urban apartments in cities like Mumbai, Delhi-NCR, Bangalore, and Hyderabad frequently suffer from cold acoustic reflections caused by smooth porcelain tiles, expansive glass windows, and concrete walls. Solid reclaimed hardwood acts as an organic acoustic diffuser and biophilic anchor. Placing solid teak root sculptures, carved deity reliefs, or tactile animal figurines immediately introduces earthy warmth, grounding the visual and sensory rhythm of the living space.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tk-home-editorial__section">
          <h3 class="tk-home-editorial__subtitle">The Alchemy of Molten Glass on Reclaimed Teak Roots</h3>
          <p>
            Our signature <em>Valley Vases</em> and molten glass on root wood installations represent the pinnacle of bespoke artisanal skill. Craftsmen gather glowing molten glass on blowpipes at temperatures surpassing 1,000°C and drape it while incandescent over seasoned teak roots. As the red-hot glass sinks into the natural grooves, knots, and hollows of the wood, it gently chars the timber surface, creating a permanent custom-fitted socket. The resulting glass vessel lifts off effortlessly for rinsing, while the sculpture remains an unrepeatable conversation centerpiece.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tk-home-editorial__section">
          <h3 class="tk-home-editorial__subtitle">Auspicious Vastu Directions for Wooden Home Decor</h3>
          <p>
            According to the foundational tenets of Vastu Shastra, natural wood belongs to the Wood and Earth elements, radiating peaceful, life-nourishing energy (Prana). 
            Placing wooden Ganesha reliefs or sacred Mukha Buddha wall art on <strong>East or North-East (Ishanya)</strong> walls invites spiritual clarity and intellect. For dining tables and living room credenzas, artisan tabletop bowls and animal figurines placed in the <strong>North (Kubera direction)</strong> attract abundance, while wooden wind chimes in the <strong>North-West (Vayu quadrant)</strong> disperse stagnant energy with resonant acoustic chimes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- COLLECTION HUBS LINKING ARCHITECTURE -->
